  "text": "Results: There were 33 patients with periacetabular osteolysis and 106 patients without. Mean follow-up time was 16.6 years (range, 12–30). 16 patients (11%) were diagnosed with CVD after a mean (SD) of 14 (6) years, with a higher relative incidence 8/33 (24%) vs 8/106 (8%) of CVD among patients with periacetabular osteolysis. The hazard ratio was 1.6, 95% confidence interval (0.4–5.8). There were no differences in presence of cardiovascular risk markers or ECG abnormalities."
